 ## Stable tier
 
 *Breaking changes require an accepted RFC and a deprecation cycle of at least
 two major versions.*
 
+### Fixed since 1.0.0-frozen — 2026-09-08
+
+- **Native backend arithmetic-error parity** (`src/jit/runtime.rs`,
+  `src/aot/mod.rs`, `src/aot/codegen.rs`). Tiered JIT arithmetic helpers now
+  report runtime faults through the JIT's existing pending-error channel
+  instead of contaminating the standalone-AOT slot; re-entrant JIT
+  save/restore preserves the correct channel; first error wins in both native
+  channels; AOT clears stale error state at each run boundary; and boxed
+  statically-Int negation retains its runtime tag check so nil-producing
+  integer operations cannot be miscompiled as zero. Deterministic regressions
+  cover the failures found by all ten shards of the 2026-09-08 differential
+  fuzz campaign.
+
 ### Added since 1.0.0-frozen — 2026-08-22 (vscode extension)
